---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/interactive.css';
import { getItems, getGuides, lanes } from '../../lib/data';
import { KIT_SOURCES } from '../../data/kit-guidance';

const items = await getItems();
const guides = await getGuides();
const catalog = {
  items: Object.fromEntries(items.map((i) => [i.id, { name: i.data.name }])),
  lanes: Object.fromEntries(lanes.map((l) => [l.slug, { name: l.name, icon: l.icon }])),
  guides: Object.fromEntries(guides.map((g) => [g.id, { title: g.data.title }])),
};
---
<Base title="Emergency Kit Builder | ReadyGearHub" description="Build a printable emergency kit checklist from Ready.gov guidance, sized to your household, with links to existing ReadyGearHub listings and lanes.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/tools/">Tools</a> / Kit builder</p>
      <h1>Emergency kit builder</h1>
      <p class="lead">A custom, printable checklist based on <a href={KIT_SOURCES.kit.url}>Ready.gov’s Build A Kit</a> guidance. Water is calculated at 1 gallon per person per day, with a 3-day minimum.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <p>After an emergency, Ready.gov notes you may need to survive on your own for several days. This tool starts at 3 days, a common baseline in Ready.gov materials, and lets you plan for longer if you want. It does not invent supplies or products — only official kit items, plus links to listings and lanes that already exist on this site.</p>
    <form class="card form no-print" id="kit-form" onsubmit="return false;">
      <div class="tool-toolbar cols-2" style="margin:0">
        <label>People in the household (including infants and children)
          <input type="number" id="kit-people" min="1" step="1" value="2" />
        </label>
        <label>Days to plan for (minimum 3)
          <input type="number" id="kit-days" min="3" step="1" value="3" />
        </label>
        <label>How many of those people are infants?
          <input type="number" id="kit-infants" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
        </label>
        <label>Pets
          <input type="number" id="kit-pets" min="0" step="1" value="0" />
        </label>
      </div>
      <label class="filter-toggle" style="width:fit-content"><input type="checkbox" id="kit-meds" /> Someone takes prescription medication or uses prescription glasses</label>
      <label class="filter-toggle" style="width:fit-content"><input type="checkbox" id="kit-vehicle" /> Include a car emergency kit</label>
      <div class="tool-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn" id="kit-print">Print or save as PDF</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <div id="kit-output" class="prose" style="max-width:none;margin-top:22px"></div>
  </section>
</Base>
<script define:vars={{ catalog }}>
  window.__rghKitCatalog = catalog;
</script>
<script>
  import { initKitBuilder } from '../../scripts/kit-builder';
  initKitBuilder((window as any).__rghKitCatalog);
</script>
